Tunl: the Firefox 148 and Safari 26.3 hellos, for metacubex/utls, the uTLS
sing-box builds with (v1.8.7 for sing-box 1.14.3). Both send an
X25519MLKEM768 key share ahead of X25519, which REALITY on Xray 26.9.8 and
later requires; Firefox 120 and Safari 16.0, which "firefox" and "safari"
named until now, send none. Xray's own client sends these two hellos.

Three commits of refraction-networking/utls, cherry-picked onto
metacubex/utls v1.8.7 in this order, their tests included:

  fc716b2d1316dbf12aa46f66916061098d6664e4  feat: add ff 148 spec and impl keyshare reuse
  ddebe3904b4d7c7f2c6c89181b349f0bb7bd1d00  fix: dont add unexported field
  aa6edf4b11af82e110eea845bb2983d30138d651  feat: add safari 26.3

The one conflict, in the imports of u_parrots.go, keeps metacubex's
internal/mlkem in place of crypto/mlkem and adds crypto/ecdh. The result is
the tree of Leadaxe/utls-lx 59e89bb, the same three commits on the same tag.
packaging/sing-box/README.md says how to reproduce it.

